# Environment Configuration key names for this Environment (ADR-0035).
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in values, or export the same keys in your shell.
# Workload Setup never reads this file — it is documentation for operators only.
#
# Manifest `environment` lists which of these keys a Workload receives.
# Prefer not to use PLATFORM_* or Credential names (e.g. DIGITALOCEAN_TOKEN) here.
# Do not list ROOT_DB_* on Manifest `environment` — those are Database admin credentials
# (ADR-0049), staged for the Database Component, not the Workload bag.
#
# Strict dotenv subset in `.env`: KEY=value, # comments / blanks, optional double quotes.
# No export, interpolation, or multiline.
#
# Database admin credentials (mandatory for Database Setup; not Workload Configuration):
ROOT_DB_USER=
ROOT_DB_PASSWORD=
#
# Taught by environments/example/env-config:
EXAMPLE_GREETING=
EXAMPLE_MODE=
